00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:17.760
Aloha, and welcome. So when we get to the end of Excel — we have four modules on Excel — then we have this project to do. The project itself is very similar to your MindTap kind of assignments,

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:31.840
except you submit it through Canvas. All right, you don't submit it through MindTap; you submit it through Canvas. And it walks you through the scenario and what you need to do.

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:54.160
The first thing you need to do is download the starter file. So right underneath the assignment instructions, you'll see this link for coastal_coffee_fall26_starter.xlsx, and you'll click on that

00:00:55.040 --> 00:01:11.040
to download it. Okay, so you'll click it to download it, and you can see over here it downloaded. And when I open it — okay, you'll have some data,

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:33.760
and you'll have two sheets. You have data in Sheet1 and some other data in Sheet2. Okay, and this is your starter data and your starter setup. And so then you will use this file to do the assignment.

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:48.000
Right, so then you'll open that file, grab it, and then you'll follow this instruction set. Okay, you download it.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:02:02.720
There is a file naming and saving and submitting part; you can click on this. It's just another — well, it should show down below. It's just another little location on the page.

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:10.320
Excel for Mac works just the same as for the PC; it shouldn't be any different. Obviously, you do this yourself.

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:22.480
You can look in here — this kind of shows you what should be in the starter file. It should match what's in the file. Here's the categories: you know, workbook setup, titles and headings, formulas and number formats,

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:43.920
quarter statistics, conditional formatting, sparklines, sales chart, espresso machine loan, and finishing and printing. So it should be something we've done across all the previous four Excel projects.

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:54.720
All right, and then you'll finish. You know, so we have all this, part by part: do this, do this, do this. And then you can do some double checks here — what your numbers should be. And if you don't match those numbers, maybe

00:02:55.840 --> 00:03:10.160
I got them wrong, or maybe you need to double-check. Okay, and then save it as Coffee_LastName_FirstName.xlsx. It has to be .xlsx — that's the only file

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:24.480
you can upload. And it's due Sunday the 15th, since you have a full week to work on it. All right, and then the grading details — here it shows the grading details: what you get points for, how many points

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:42.000
it's worth. The whole thing's worth 200 points. Okay, so, um, I think that covers it. If you have questions, obviously send me messages or make an appointment so that I can help you resolve them.

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:54.400
All right, so we're almost done. We only have PowerPoint and then Outlook to do after this, and I think you'll find those go rather smoothly —

00:03:55.360 --> 00:04:07.280
or typically those go rather smoothly for everybody. There are some differences for Outlook: we don't have projects in Outlook; it's more of an exam,

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:24.800
and you'll see that when we get there. But it's really not that, um, cumbersome, if you will. For most people it goes pretty smoothly at this point. All right, good luck, and I'll talk to you next week.
